# Help text (docs/tooltip-plan.md): the third universal prop, read back from
# the PLATFORM — the tooltip GTK and WinUI hold on the control, the
# accessibility help Apple's `.help` lands on — never from kaya's model.
expect_title "tooltips"
expect_help button#0 "Saves the draft to disk"
expect_help entry#0 "Your full name as it appears on the card"
expect_help slider#0 "How loud the preview plays"
# The column carries help too (the prop is universal), but a SwiftUI
# contained group publishes no help attribute on the Mac (measured
# 2026-09-05, docs/tooltip-plan.md §6), so its bubble is a capture's to
# witness, not this verb's.
# An authored hint wins the hint slot where a platform has one (T3): this
# button declares both, and the reader hears the hint.
expect_ax_hint button#1 "discard every change"
# An empty help hides the tooltip a button takes from its name
# (docs/tooltip-plan.md T6).
expect_help button#2 ""
# A BOUND help follows its signal: button#0's handler rewrites entry#0's.
click button#0
expect_help entry#0 "Your name, as saved"
# The template zone: a stamped label's help is the row's own field. Copies
# are addressed by INDEX with SOURCED ids, as a11yrows does: the Apple read
# goes through the accessibility identifier, and copies sharing one id
# cannot be told apart there.
expect_help label#2 "The first account, opened in March"
expect_help label#last "The second account, opened in May"
# A label cut short with an ellipsis shows its whole text as its tooltip on
# the desktops, and the same label shown whole shows none
# (docs/tooltip-plan.md T7).
expect_help label@cut "Every statement since March"
expect_help label@whole ""
# The bubble drawn at the target's centre (docs/tooltip-plan.md §6): the
# innermost help wins, and a widget with none of its own, or one that opted
# out, shows its container's.
expect_tooltip label@cut "Every statement since March"
expect_tooltip label#2 "The first account, opened in March"
expect_tooltip button#0 "Saves the draft to disk"
expect_tooltip label@whole "The settings for this account"
expect_tooltip button#2 "The settings for this account"
